.0%"},{"id":6,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"短期流動性安全 (ΔLiquidity > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"流動比率 = 2.42"},{"id":7,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"股本未遭稀釋 (ΔShares ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"未大幅增發新股割韭菜"},{"id":8,"category":"營運效率","desc":"毛利率擴張 (ΔMargin > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"產品定價權增強，毛利結構健康"},{"id":9,"category":"營運效率","desc":"資產週轉率提升 (ΔTurnover > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"每單位資產產出效益改善"}],"fair_val":45.14,"default_fair_val":45.14,"premium_pct":1.7,"is_undervalued":false,"pe_trailing":24,"pe_forward":21.1,"pb_trailing":4.1,"pb_forward":3.7,"div_yield":0,"ps_ratio":8.5,"fcf_to_ev":2.67,"fcf_to_mcap":2.95,"liab_to_assets":58,"cash_to_assets":17,"current_ratio":2.42,"roe":0,"roa":0,"moat":{"ticker":"ALKS","period":"2026Q3","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":5,"comment_zh":"Alkermes 在藥品製造領域的品牌定價權相對有限。雖然其部分藥品，如 Vivitrol 和 Aristada，在特定治療領域具有一定的市場地位，但其品牌影響力並非如消費品般強大，難以形成顯著的溢價能力。面對其他藥廠的同類產品或替代療法，Alkermes 的定價彈性受到限制。其營收主要依賴於藥品銷售，而非強勢品牌所帶來的持續性高利潤率，因此在品牌定價權方面，其護城河僅為中等水平。","comment_en":"Alkermes has limited brand pricing power within the drug manufacturing sector. While some of its drugs, such as Vivitrol and Aristada, hold a certain market position in specific therapeutic areas, its brand influence is not as potent as that of consumer goods, making it difficult to command significant premium pricing. Facing similar products or alternative therapies from other pharmaceutical companies, Alkermes' pricing flexibility is constrained. Its revenue primarily relies on drug sales rather than the sustained high profit margins associated with strong brands, thus its moat in terms of brand pricing power is only moderate."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Alkermes 的核心競爭力在於其藥品專利和監管壁壘。公司在神經科學和腫瘤學領域擁有專利保護的藥品，這些專利為其產品提供了獨占市場的機會，並在一定時期內阻止了競爭對手的仿製。此外，藥品研發和上市過程本身就涉及極高的監管門檻和漫長的審批週期，這對新進入者構成了巨大的挑戰。雖然專利終將到期，但其在專利保護期內形成的市場優勢是顯著的。","comment_en":"Alkermes' core competitive strength lies in its drug patents and regulatory barriers. The company possesses patented drugs in the fields of neuroscience and oncology, which grant them exclusive market opportunities and prevent generic competition for a certain period. Furthermore, the drug development and approval process itself involves extremely high regulatory hurdles and lengthy review cycles, posing significant challenges for new entrants. Although patents eventually expire, the market advantage established during the patent protection period is substantial."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"在醫療保健領域，患者和醫生對於藥品的轉換成本相對較高。一旦患者開始使用某種藥物並產生療效，或醫生習慣於開立某種處方，轉換到另一種藥物的意願和可行性都會降低，因為需要考慮療效的連續性、潛在的副作用以及重新評估的成本。Alkermes 的藥品，特別是針對慢性病或複雜疾病的藥物，在一定程度上受益於這種轉換成本，但這並非絕對，因為醫療決策仍會受到療效、安全性及成本效益的影響。","comment_en":"In the healthcare sector, the switching costs for patients and physicians regarding medications are relatively high. Once a patient begins a course of treatment with a particular drug and experiences efficacy, or a physician becomes accustomed to prescribing a certain medication, the willingness and feasibility of switching to another drug decrease due to considerations of treatment continuity, potential side effects, and the cost of re-evaluation. Alkermes' drugs, particularly those for chronic or complex diseases, benefit to some extent from these switching costs, although this is not absolute, as medical decisions are still influenced by efficacy, safety, and cost-effectiveness."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"Alkermes 的業務模式，即藥品研發和銷售，本質上不具備顯著的網絡效應。其產品的成功主要取決於藥物的療效、安全性、臨床試驗數據以及市場推廣，而非用戶之間的互動或連接所產生的價值增長。與社交媒體或電商平台不同，Alkermes 的客戶（患者和醫生）之間不存在直接的網絡效應，因此這一維度上的護城河非常薄弱。","comment_en":"Alkermes' business model, which involves drug research, development, and sales, inherently lacks significant network effects. The success of its products primarily depends on drug efficacy, safety, clinical trial data, and marketing, rather than value growth generated from user interactions or connections. Unlike social media or e-commerce platforms, there are no direct network effects among Alkermes' customers (patients and physicians), making the moat in this dimension very weak."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":5,"comment_zh":"Alkermes 在藥品生產和研發方面，相較於大型製藥巨頭，其規模優勢並不突出。雖然公司在特定治療領域擁有一定的生產能力，但與那些擁有全球化生產網絡和龐大採購量的競爭對手相比，其在單位生產成本上的優勢有限。研發投入雖然巨大，但其規模效應的體現不如那些能夠通過多元化產品線攤薄研發成本的公司。因此，在成本優勢方面，其護城河僅為中等。","comment_en":"In terms of drug manufacturing and R&D, Alkermes does not possess a prominent scale advantage compared to major pharmaceutical giants. While the company has certain production capabilities in specific therapeutic areas, its advantage in unit production costs is limited when compared to competitors with global manufacturing networks and massive procurement volumes. Although R&D investments are substantial, the realization of economies of scale is less pronounced than in companies that can spread R&D costs across diversified product lines. Therefore, its moat in terms of cost advantage is only moderate."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":3,"comment_zh":"Alkermes 的業務主要集中在藥品研發和銷售，其核心資產是知識產權和研發能力，而非獨特的地理位置或實物資產。雖然公司在全球範圍內進行藥品銷售，但其營運並未依賴於任何特定的地理優勢或稀缺資源。其競爭優勢更多體現在技術和專利上，而非地理位置帶來的獨特性，因此在這一維度上護城河較弱。","comment_en":"Alkermes' business primarily focuses on drug R&D and sales, with its core assets being intellectual property and R&D capabilities, rather than unique geographical locations or physical assets. Although the company sells drugs globally, its operations do not rely on any specific geographical advantages or scarce resources. Its competitive advantages are more evident in technology and patents, rather than uniqueness derived from location, thus the moat in this dimension is weak."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Alkermes 在其藥品研發、臨床試驗管理和生產流程方面展現了一定的營運效率。公司能夠相對有效地推進其研發管線，並將產品推向市場。然而，與行業內頂尖的製藥公司相比，其營運效率的領先程度並不明顯。藥品行業本身就面臨著嚴格的監管和高昂的成本，Alkermes 在此環境下維持穩定的營運已屬不易，但要說其擁有顯著的超額營運效率作為護城河，則尚有提升空間。","comment_en":"Alkermes demonstrates a certain level of operational efficiency in its drug R&D, clinical trial management, and production processes. The company can advance its R&D pipeline and bring products to market relatively effectively. However, compared to the top pharmaceutical companies in the industry, its operational efficiency is not significantly superior. The pharmaceutical industry itself faces stringent regulations and high costs, and it is commendable for Alkermes to maintain stable operations under these circumstances. However, to claim it possesses a significant excess operational efficiency as a moat, there is still room for improvement."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Alkermes 的資本配置能力是其重要的競爭優勢之一。公司在研發投入、潛在的併購以及股東回報之間進行權衡。儘管過去的 ROE 和 ROA 數據不佳，但其自由現金流（FCF TTM: $227.4M）顯示其具備一定的造血能力。管理層需要持續有效地將資本投入到高潛力研發項目和戰略性收購中，以維持其增長軌跡並提升股東價值。其在有限資源下尋求高回報的策略，是其護城河的體現。","comment_en":"Alkermes' capital allocation capability is one of its significant competitive advantages. The company balances investments in R&D, potential M&A, and shareholder returns. Despite past poor ROE and ROA figures, its Free Cash Flow (FCF TTM: $227.4M) indicates a certain ability to generate cash. Management needs to continuously and effectively deploy capital into high-potential R&D projects and strategic acquisitions to sustain its growth trajectory and enhance shareholder value. Its strategy of seeking high returns with limited resources is a manifestation of its moat."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Alkermes 的客戶主要是醫療機構和患者，其客戶留存率在一定程度上受到藥品療效和醫生處方習慣的影響。對於慢性病治療藥物，一旦患者病情穩定且藥物有效，轉換的可能性較低。然而，藥品市場的競爭激烈，新藥的出現、治療指南的更新以及價格因素都可能影響客戶的選擇。因此，Alkermes 的客戶留存並非基於強烈的品牌忠誠度或網絡效應，而是更多地依賴於產品本身的臨床價值和醫生推薦，屬於中等水平的護城河。","comment_en":"Alkermes' customers are primarily healthcare providers and patients, and its customer retention rate is influenced to some extent by drug efficacy and physician prescribing habits. For chronic disease treatment drugs, once a patient's condition is stable and the medication is effective, the likelihood of switching is lower. However, the pharmaceutical market is highly competitive, and the emergence of new drugs, updates in treatment guidelines, and pricing factors can all affect customer choices. Therefore, Alkermes' customer retention is not based on strong brand loyalty or network effects but rather relies more on the clinical value of the product itself and physician recommendations, representing a moderate level of moat."},"m10_durability":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Alkermes 的業務具有一定的持久性，這主要得益於其在神經科學和腫瘤學領域的專利保護藥品。這些藥品在專利期內能夠提供穩定的收入來源。然而，製藥行業的技術迭代和監管變化快速，專利的到期是其業務持久性面臨的主要挑戰。公司需要不斷投入研發以補充其產品管線，確保長期競爭力。其現有產品組合的持久性中等，依賴於持續的創新和專利續期。","comment_en":"Alkermes' business possesses a degree of durability, primarily due to its patented drugs in the fields of neuroscience and oncology. These drugs can provide a stable revenue stream during their patent life. However, the pharmaceutical industry is characterized by rapid technological iteration and regulatory changes, and patent expiration is the main challenge to its business durability. The company needs to continuously invest in R&D to replenish its product pipeline and ensure long-term competitiveness. The durability of its existing product portfolio is moderate, relying on continuous innovation and patent extensions."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"Alkermes 的經濟護城河主要建立在其藥品專利和監管壁壘（M2）以及一定的客戶轉換成本（M3）之上。公司在特定治療領域的藥品具有一定的市場地位，並受益於研發投入和資本配置能力（M8）。然而，其品牌定價權（M1）、規模成本（M5）、網絡效應（M4）和地理資產（M6）相對薄弱。業務的持久性（M10）和客戶留存（M9）處於中等水平，依賴於持續的創新和臨床價值。整體而言，Alkermes 處於一個競爭激烈且受監管嚴格的行業，其護城河雖具備一定強度，但並非堅不可摧的特許經營權，更接近於一個依賴專利和研發的技術型公司。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"Alkermes' economic moat is primarily built upon its drug patents and regulatory barriers (M2) and certain customer switching costs (M3). The company's drugs in specific therapeutic areas hold a certain market position and benefit from R&D investment and capital allocation capabilities (M8). However, its brand pricing power (M1), cost advantages from scale (M5), network effects (M4), and geographical assets (M6) are relatively weak. Business durability (M10) and customer retention (M9) are at a moderate level, dependent on continuous innovation and clinical value. Overall, Alkermes operates in a highly competitive and strictly regulated industry. While its moat possesses some strength, it is not an unassailable franchise; it more closely resembles a technology-driven company reliant on patents and R&D.","evidenceHash":"da3d055a3232975031bf5b333b94a0d88eb6255c0dadfa4e2874ea848ac6a9a2","assessmentPolicy":"buffett-moat-v3","model":"gemini-2.5-flash-lite","provider":"Vertex AI"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":"staleEvidence","evidenceHash":"da3d055a3232975031bf5b333b94a0d88eb6255c0dadfa4e2874ea848ac6a9a2","currentEvidenceHash":"03b2aa2e3f65bea949da4745502892c6cd75aa1678e7d188a89d8fb95a04667e"},"fScore":{"score":5,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"superRobust","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-07T07:50:10.998Z","evidenceHash":"d5041dcf0eb11f2afc7e1df68728e7720a95c051997968eac7afd3a64f438118"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"clean","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-07T07:50:10.998Z","evidenceHash":"d5041dcf0eb11f2afc7e1df68728e7720a95c051997968eac7afd3a64f438118"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/ALKS.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/ALKS.png","website":"http://www.alkermes.com","ceo":"Blair Jackson","full_time_employees":"2050","description":"Alkermes plc, a biopharmaceutical company, engages in the research, development, and commercialization of pharmaceutical products to address unmet medical needs of patients in therapeutic areas in the United States, Ireland, and internationally. The company has a portfolio of proprietary commercial products for the treatment of opioid dependence, alcohol dependence, schizophrenia, bipolar I, and a pipeline of clinical and preclinical product candidates in development for neurological disorders. Its marketed products include ARISTADA, an intramuscular injectable suspension for the treatment of schizophrenia; ARISTADA INITIO for the treatment of schizophrenia in adults; VIVITROL for the treatment of alcohol and prevention of opioid dependence; LYBALVI, an oral atypical antipsychotic drug candidate for the treatment of adults with schizophrenia and bipolar I disorder; and LUMRYZ, an extended-release oral suspension product for the treatment of cataplexy or EDS in pediatric patients. The company also offers proprietary technology platforms to third parties to enable them to develop, commercialize, and manufacture products. It has collaboration agreements primarily with Janssen Pharmaceutica N.V., Janssen Pharmaceutica Inc, and Janssen Pharmaceutica International. Alkermes plc was founded in 1987 and is headquartered in Dublin, Ireland.","description_en":"Alkermes plc, a biopharmaceutical company, engages in the research, development, and commercialization of pharmaceutical products to address unmet medical needs of patients in therapeutic areas in the United States, Ireland, and internationally. The company has a portfolio of proprietary commercial products for the treatment of opioid dependence, alcohol dependence, schizophrenia, bipolar I, and a pipeline of clinical and preclinical product candidates in development for neurological disorders. Its marketed products include ARISTADA, an intramuscular injectable suspension for the treatment of schizophrenia; ARISTADA INITIO for the treatment of schizophrenia in adults; VIVITROL for the treatment of alcohol and prevention of opioid dependence; LYBALVI, an oral atypical antipsychotic drug candidate for the treatment of adults with schizophrenia and bipolar I disorder; and LUMRYZ, an extended-release oral suspension product for the treatment of cataplexy or EDS in pediatric patients. The company also offers proprietary technology platforms to third parties to enable them to develop, commercialize, and manufacture products. It has collaboration agreements primarily with Janssen Pharmaceutica N.V., Janssen Pharmaceutica Inc, and Janssen Pharmaceutica International. Alkermes plc was founded in 1987 and is headquartered in Dublin, Ireland.","description_zh":"Alkermes plc（美股代碼：ALKS）為 Healthcare 領域之重要企業，專注於 Drug Manufacturers - Specialty & Generic 業務，具備清晰之商業壁壘與現金流創造能力。","address":"Connaught House","city":"Dublin","state":"DU","zip":"D04 C5Y6","country":"IE","phone":"353 1 772 8000","full_address":"Connaught House, Dublin, DU D04 C5Y6, IE","range_52w":"27-55.67","year_high":55.67,"year_low":27,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":27,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[{"date":"2026-11-03","name":"Gaffin David Joseph","title":"officer: EVP, CLO, Alkermes, Inc.","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":2035,"price":46.17,"total_val":0.09},{"date":"2026-10-09","name":"Reed Joshua","title":"officer: SVP, Chief Financial Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":9164,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-09","name":"Reed Joshua","title":"officer: SVP, Chief Financial Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":9164,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-09","name":"Reed Joshua","title":"officer: SVP, Chief Financial Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"F-InKind","shares":4069,"price":40.11,"total_val":0.16},{"date":"2026-10-09","name":"Whitaker Anne Clem","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":17998,"price":41.45,"total_val":0.75},{"date":"2026-10-09","name":"Whitaker Anne Clem","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":7239,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-02","name":"Gaffin David Joseph","title":"officer: EVP, CLO, Alkermes, Inc.","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":2034,"price":41.03,"total_val":0.08},{"date":"2026-09-18","name":"Whitaker Anne Clem","title":"directo